  "details": "This was another request mentioned not by me, but by the community.\n\nAdding in some sort of metric, frametime is just what was easiest to convey.\n\nThis metric counts the avatar performance stat by how much it affects the frametime or FPS. \n\nI know this is not easy, and may be better alternatives but it should help identify what avatars are causing performance issues in large instances. Much the same way imposter generation computes on the cloud, maybe have some sort of check run online that validates performance somehow in a controlled medium and allow users to click a button to re run the test upon upload.",
